 place (granted or rented), and offering corresponding source from
 the same place through a designated network place, valid for at
 least three years and valid for as long as you offer access from
 the designated place.  The designated network place must be one
 that is widely used and accessible to the public, and the
 Corresponding Source must be available at least as long as the
 object code is offered from the designated place.

 e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer transmission,
 provided you inform other peers of the object code and the
 Corresponding Source.  The Corresponding Source must be available
 at least as long as the object code is available.

 A separable portion of the object code whose source code is excluded
 from the Corresponding Source because it is not part of the user
 interface is called a System Library, and the Independent
 Use/Exclusive Use exception does not apply to it.

